# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_tauri_command_contract.py" "TAURI COMMAND CONTRACT GATE: PASS" "Tauri command-contract coupling: Rust command definitions plus official frontend invoke calls" "Tauri command contract substrate: a Rust tauri command definition and an official frontend invoke call to the same literal command name are coupled through a shared tauri_command key with no direct import or call edge between src-tauri and frontend source. Precision guards: frontend references require invoke imported from the official Tauri API module, dynamic names do not emit, comment-only mentions do not emit, plain Rust functions do not mint commands, and duplicate command definers are dropped as ambiguous. Content-free: command names, file paths, and edge kinds only; body and comment strings never appear in graph output. Additive: non-Tauri repos produce no tauri_command nodes or edges. Gate 226." "Tauri command contract substrate recovers a narrow AI-era src-to-src-tauri cross-dir coupling while preserving content-free precision: official invoke literal plus single Rust tauri command definition only; local invoke, dynamic names, comments, plain functions, and duplicate definers stay silent." 20
